From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AudioPulse: terminate the executable path before taking
 its basename

readlink() does not write a terminating NUL, and AudioPulse's
constructor handed the buffer straight to basename() and strcpy(). What
follows the path in exePath is uninitialised stack, so the PulseAudio
client name could pick up garbage, and with no zero byte before the end
of the buffer both calls would read past it and strcpy() would write
past exeName. valgrind reports it on every AudioPulse construction:

  Conditional jump or move depends on uninitialised value(s)
     at rindex / basename
     by tgvoip::audio::AudioPulse::AudioPulse(...)

Read at most sizeof(exePath)-1 bytes, terminate the result, and copy the
basename with snprintf() bounded by exeName.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp b/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp
index f02ece8..0ba4084 100644
--- a/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp
+++ b/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp
@@ -144,13 +144,15 @@ AudioPulse::AudioPulse(std::string inputDevice, std::string outputDevice){
 #else
 	char exePath[MAXPATHLEN];
 	char exeName[MAXPATHLEN];
-	ssize_t lres=readlink("/proc/self/exe", exePath, sizeof(exePath));
+	// readlink() does not terminate what it returns; leave room for the terminator.
+	ssize_t lres=readlink("/proc/self/exe", exePath, sizeof(exePath)-1);
 	if(lres==-1)
-		lres=readlink("/proc/curproc/file", exePath, sizeof(exePath));
+		lres=readlink("/proc/curproc/file", exePath, sizeof(exePath)-1);
 	if(lres==-1)
-		lres=readlink("/proc/curproc/exe", exePath, sizeof(exePath));
+		lres=readlink("/proc/curproc/exe", exePath, sizeof(exePath)-1);
 	if(lres>0){
-		strcpy(exeName, basename(exePath));
+		exePath[lres]=0;
+		snprintf(exeName, sizeof(exeName), "%s", basename(exePath));
 	}else
 #endif
 	{
